    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "okay so u say the inequality part is the \"undeniable legacy\" and \"more definitive.\" is that because the growth arguments are basically just theoretical or outdated? like, does most current econ research actually reject the idea that deregulation was a net positive?",
      "source": "evaluator"
