      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is more accurate to say the strong evidence for rising inequality is more consistent across a broader range of modern analyses, rather than the 1980s growth argument being entirely \"out of date.\" Many current and conservative modern economic views don't outright \"reject\" the idea of a positive outcome, but they strongly challenge the view that the benefits of that growth were broadly and equally shared across the entire population, making the inequality a central, well-supported critique.",
